# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# downloaded dataset files (regenerated on first run)
data/
mnist/

# arXiv e-print unpack under paper/source/: track ONLY the LaTeX/bibliography
# sources (.tex/.bbl/.bib) — the authoritative maths reference. Figures
# (.png/.pdf), style files (.sty/.bst) and the eprint tarball are ignored:
# they are not reproduced from and bloat every clone. Files may remain
# unpacked on disk for local reference.
paper/source/*
!paper/source/*.tex
!paper/source/*.bbl
!paper/source/*.bib
*.tar.gz
eprint*

# self-check grader output is reproducible via selfcheck_claims.py, but it is
# the evidence a reader checks our self-claimed verdicts against, so it is
# COMMITTED (not gitignored) -- a number whose output file is ignored is a
# claim with its evidence deleted.
#
# claims_result.json is the workflow's numbers-gate verdict table. The
# workflow writes it and we commit it; it must NEVER be gitignored (a
# reproduction without it in the repo has published its summary and withheld
# its evidence). It is absent now only because the publish step has not run.
